content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite)",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 7.6 mm/s. The limit is the HF-300 Figure 3 vibration severity chart: Zone D runs from 7.1 mm/s RMS upward and is labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The reading is 0.5 mm/s above the Zone C/D boundary, so it is not a boundary case. The manual says to classify the highest bearing-housing reading and act on its zone. The site standard says vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone requires an immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 84 C. The limit is the HF-300 data table: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, trip at 90 C. The reading is 4 C above alarm and 6 C below trip. The site standard requires a priority-1 work order within the shift when bearing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal leakage is about 1 drop per second. The HF-300 manual troubleshooting table lists 'Leakage at shaft seal' as a symptom requiring mechanical seal replacement. The documents give no numeric acceptable leak rate.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The pump ran dry for about 10 minutes last week. The manual requires a Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and states the pump must never run dry, so this operation breached the manufacturer's requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal faces were damaged by last week's 10-minute dry run, causing the shaft leak. 'Seal run dry' is a listed cause of seal leakage. The fitted seal type is unknown; if the original HF3-450 component seal is fitted, the service bulletin also reports early field failures of that seal on serials HF3-22000 and above.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is the only cause listed for all three symptoms: seal leakage, high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear, which is consistent with both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation, possibly linked to the dry-run or tank-changeover event.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the drive-end bearing, a listed cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 immediately because vibration is in Zone D. Notify the reliability engineer. Do not restart without the reliability engineer's approval.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump: electrical LOTO at the MCC, close and lock the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit. Drain and vent the pump before opening it. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because the line is hypochlorite-dosed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before lifting, prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and arrange certified lifting equipment. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which is above the 25 kg site threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, then remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller and wear rings for damage or imbalance.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the mechanical seal and shaft sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450 on this serial. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect both bearings and check grease quantity. The drive-end housing exceeded its alarm temperature, so replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end 6312-C3 (HF3-512) and non-drive-end 6310-C3 (HF3-510).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble with lightly oiled threads and tighten to these torques: seal gland nuts (M10) 30 Nm per SB-2026-014, not 25 Nm; impeller nut (M24) 160 Nm; casing bolts (M16) 210 Nm; bearing housing bolts (M12) 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the pump and motor after the bearing housing work. Tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the casing is full and the Plan 11 seal flush is working; the pump must never run dry. With the reliability engineer's approval, restart. Then measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3. Confirm bearing housing temperature stays within the normal range of 70 C or below.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set; supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (bearings replaced as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (bearings replaced as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; contingent, fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the machine immediately (vibration is in Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone) and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Raise as a priority-1 work order within the shift, because bearing temperature of 84 C exceeds the 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; line-break permit with drain and vent first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves, because P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line are dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sum of the standard times is 11.5 h. The actual total may be lower if seal and bearing work share the back pull-out disassembly; the documents do not say.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list specifies HF3-450 (component seal), but SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says do not fit HF3-450 on HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above; use HF3-450B. P-104 is serial HF3-22871, which is within the bulletin range. The bulletin is the later document and specific to this serial range, so HF3-450B applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, but SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin states that only pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use Table 5. P-104 (HF3-22871) therefore uses 30 Nm. All other Table 5 torques still apply, as the bulletin does not change them.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling: the manual only says to inspect the sleeve for scoring. The bulletin adds a replacement criterion of 0.1 mm scoring depth and says no sleeve measurement is needed for setting HF3-450B. The bulletin criterion applies to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the 7.6 mm/s reading RMS? Figure 3 is in mm/s RMS, but the report does not state the measurement type.",
    "No non-drive-end vibration or temperature reading was reported. The manual requires measuring both housings.",
    "Which seal is currently fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B) and when was it installed?",
    "Grease type, grease quantity and relubrication interval for the bearings are not given in the evidence.",
    "Part numbers for wear rings, and a spare impeller decision if the impeller is damaged, are not covered beyond impeller HF3-210 in the parts list.",
    "Combined labour time when seal and bearing replacement are done in one disassembly is not documented.",
    "What controls (e.g. low-level or dry-run protection) will prevent a repeat dry run during tank changeovers? Not covered by the evidence.",
    "Decontamination requirements for hypochlorite-wetted parts beyond goggles and gloves are not specified.",
    "Stock availability of HF3-450B and the other listed parts is not known."
  ]
}
